64
00:06:23,540 --> 00:06:27,240
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: When we speak of poverty, we usually speak of income.

65
00:06:27,460 --> 00:06:33,260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We speak of the ability of every family to afford food, secure decent work,

66
00:06:33,580 --> 00:06:37,980
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: access essential services, and pursue a better life.

67
00:06:38,420 --> 00:06:46,500
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: There is, however, one dimension of poverty we tend to overlook, the poverty of security.

68
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:55,100
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: To my fellow lawmakers, peace, safety, disaster, resilience, and the capacity of our local government units

69
00:06:55,100 --> 00:07:00,680
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: to deliver basic necessities are not expenses that compete with economic development.

70
00:07:01,290 --> 00:07:05,340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: They are the conditions which make economic development possible.

71
00:07:05,340 --> 00:07:09,040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Congress therefore supports the Department's direction

72
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:12,860
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: towards safer, more resilient communities,

73
00:07:13,540 --> 00:07:20,860
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: stronger local governments, and law enforcement institutions that are trusted, capable, and responsive.

74
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:28,820
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: This is precisely why the DILG's requested budget of P332.5 billion

75
00:07:28,820 --> 00:07:34,680
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: under the fiscal year 2027 National Expenditure Program.

76
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:37,720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: 7.1% higher than

77
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:42,740
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: the Fiscal Year 2026 General Appropriations Act level

78
00:07:42,740 --> 00:07:52,060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: will be a strategic public commitment that should yield clear and measurable returns in peace and order,

79
00:07:52,480 --> 00:07:57,220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: public safety, disaster preparedness, and local governance.

80
00:07:57,220 --> 00:08:01,780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: It will provide sustained institutional support for the department

81
00:08:01,780 --> 00:08:08,920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and will convert national policy into peace, safety, security, and services

82
00:08:08,920 --> 00:08:12,460
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: at the level where Filipinos actually experience government.

83
00:08:12,460 --> 00:08:21,040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Of the total proposal, P242.5 billion is intended for the Philippine National Police,

84
00:08:21,360 --> 00:08:28,000
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: underscoring its central role of effective policing and maintaining a secure domestic environment.

85
00:08:28,620 --> 00:08:33,780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Over the past year, the DILG has delivered significant gains in public safety,

86
00:08:34,100 --> 00:08:37,960
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: law enforcement, corrections, and local governance.

87
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:46,500
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The department posted a 96.33 efficiency rate in emergency response

88
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:50,440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: with response times of 5 to 7 minutes.

89
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:57,240
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: As we enter the rainy season, we now have 50,441 evacuation centers nationwide

90
00:08:57,620 --> 00:09:05,080
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: with more than 126,000 uniformed personnel deployed for disaster response

91
00:09:05,460 --> 00:09:07,860
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: ready to assist Filipinos in distress,

92
00:09:08,160 --> 00:09:10,860
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: especially in light of the recent Habagat.

93
00:09:10,860 --> 00:09:13,740
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The crime rate has continued to go down

94
00:09:13,760 --> 00:09:17,280
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: with lower numbers across focused crimes,

95
00:09:17,740 --> 00:09:19,920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: index and non-index crimes,

96
00:09:20,180 --> 00:09:22,240
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and cybercrimes cases.

97
00:09:22,740 --> 00:09:25,020
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: These gains deserve sustained support,

98
00:09:25,300 --> 00:09:31,060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: especially as the threat environment continues to evolve.

99
00:09:31,920 --> 00:09:35,940
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Recent incidents of school and academic violence involving students,

100
00:09:36,400 --> 00:09:37,640
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: together with threats

101
00:09:37,640 --> 00:09:39,720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: circulated through online platforms,

102
00:09:39,720 --> 00:09:42,480
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: create a new challenge for the PNP

103
00:09:42,480 --> 00:09:46,740
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and other law enforcement agencies with related mandates.

104
00:09:47,040 --> 00:09:56,540
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The PNP's report of 50 school-related incidents involving minors from June 16 to August 18, 2026

105
00:09:56,540 --> 00:10:02,820
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: reinforces the need for prevention, early detection, rapid response,

106
00:10:02,820 --> 00:10:08,020
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and responsible digital monitoring that respects lawful safeguards.

107
00:10:08,020 --> 00:10:09,040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: In this regard,

108
00:10:09,260 --> 00:10:14,300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: we welcome and support the Department's review of school security protocols,

109
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:18,840
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: the strengthening of safer school zones,

110
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:21,980
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: closer DILG-DepEd coordination,

111
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:25,000
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and active police-community partnership,

112
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:29,360
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: including mobilization of barangay peace and safety mechanisms.

113
00:10:29,360 --> 00:10:33,400
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The proposed budget provides concrete support through

114
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:36,800
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: P3.1 billion for PNP

115
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:40,600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: information and communication technologies projects,

116
00:10:40,940 --> 00:10:46,600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: P2 billion for the PNP capability enhancement program,

117
00:10:46,920 --> 00:10:55,420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and P48.95 million for Phase 2 of the Philippine Public Safety College National Cyber Training Institute.

118
00:10:55,420 --> 00:10:59,660
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: These resources should translate into trained investigators,

119
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:02,780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: stronger digital forensics capability,

120
00:11:03,240 --> 00:11:06,600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: secure and interoperable systems,

121
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:10,840
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: practical threat reporting channels,

122
00:11:11,140 --> 00:11:14,820
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and clear response protocols for schools and communities.

123
00:11:14,820 --> 00:11:17,400
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: According to the United Nations,

124
00:11:17,880 --> 00:11:21,300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: peace is not simply the absence of conflict.

125
00:11:21,520 --> 00:11:26,180
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: It is the foundation on which all sustainable development is built.

126
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:29,480
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: No less than the President himself said in his SONA

127
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:34,640
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: that our goal as a government is to uplift the lives of struggling Filipinos.

128
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:38,840
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: If our objective is to uplift the poor,

129
00:11:38,940 --> 00:11:42,860
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: we must make sure places where Filipinos live are safe,

130
00:11:43,100 --> 00:11:46,520
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: orderly, and resilient with their local governments

131
00:11:46,520 --> 00:11:50,540
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: capable of responding immediately when crisis strikes.

132
00:11:50,540 --> 00:11:54,300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The DILG's budget affirms our shared commitment

133
00:11:54,300 --> 00:11:57,380
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: to strengthen the government's capacity to act.

134
00:11:57,840 --> 00:12:03,380
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Communities in crisis need a government capable of responding today,

135
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:04,860
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: not tomorrow.

136
00:12:04,860 --> 00:12:06,660
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Our shared challenge

137
00:12:06,660 --> 00:12:10,900
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: is to help the Department move these reforms forward

138
00:12:10,900 --> 00:12:15,140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: while ensuring that every appropriation is used

139
00:12:15,140 --> 00:12:19,300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: strategically, promptly, and accountably to prevent threats,

140
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:23,460
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: protect the vulnerable, and preserve peaceful communities.

141
00:12:24,180 --> 00:12:30,620
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Congress stands ready to support Secretary Remulla and the entire DILG family

142
00:12:30,620 --> 00:12:34,920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: in advancing programs that strengthen peace and order

143
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:38,640
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and allow our people's school, business, and local economies

144
00:12:38,640 --> 00:12:39,180
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: to thrive.

145
00:12:39,180 --> 00:12:44,180
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We must protect our constituents' right to safety and security.

146
00:12:44,560 --> 00:12:46,960
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: When our communities are peaceful,

147
00:12:47,260 --> 00:12:50,960
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: our constituents are put in a better position for growth,

148
00:12:51,140 --> 00:12:53,720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: prosperity, and meaningful development.

149
00:12:54,240 --> 00:12:57,060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Secretary Remulla, we look forward to your presentation.

150
00:12:57,600 --> 00:13:00,520
