05:46:15,201 --> 05:46:22,480
BJMP Chief Jail Director Efren A. Nemeño: But hindi po ito, Your Honor, na pupunta yung bisita doon na hindi nag-request yung PDL natin.

6591
05:46:25,060 --> 05:46:34,680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Well, Chair, ito nga yung nakakarating sa amin na ulat na kakaiba yung patakaran nyo with regard to non-direct family members.

6592
05:46:36,760 --> 05:46:41,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At ang sinabi rin sa akin na hindi ganito ang patakaran ng BuCor, halimbawa.

6593
05:46:41,740 --> 05:46:50,240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Na mas kayo pa, BJMP, ang may napaka-strictong patakaran na mainly direct family ang puwede.

6594
05:46:51,010 --> 05:46:54,900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero may iba pang requirements kapag hindi direct.

6595
05:46:55,140 --> 05:46:56,720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ngayon, bakit issue to?

6596
05:46:57,760 --> 05:47:06,600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Marami pong may mga kaso po na mayroon tayong mga detainees na hindi maaaring nasa ibang isla, malayo.

6597
05:47:06,601 --> 05:47:15,080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang kanilang direct family, ibig sabihin kahit talimbawa best friend ka, kababata mo, hindi basta-bastang pwede mong bisitahin.

6598
05:47:15,160 --> 05:47:20,620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ganun po ang inuulat sa amin.

6599
05:47:21,660 --> 05:47:28,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Mga konkretong instances sa Bohol at saka sa Negros, ganun daw po.

6600
05:47:30,820 --> 05:47:35,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At sinasabi rin na ang BuCor hindi ganun, mas mahigpit pa kayo sa BuCor.

6601
05:47:35,940 --> 05:47:37,280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bakit ko hina-highlight ito?

6602
05:47:37,360 --> 05:47:40,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, sa BuCor, alam natin, iyon ay para sa mga convicted.

6603
05:47:43,240 --> 05:47:50,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Whereas ang BJMP, detainees, innocent until proven guilty in the end. Diba?

6604
05:47:51,480 --> 05:47:54,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So bakit po, mas mahigpit pa kayo?

6605
05:47:55,420 --> 05:47:59,860
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At hindi ba ito paglabag sa karapatan?

6606
05:48:00,400 --> 05:48:05,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Parang inhuman, cruel and inhuman.

6607
05:48:05,021 --> 05:48:11,480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Na naghihigpit kayo sa karapatan na mabisita, kahit ng hindi direct family.

6608
05:48:11,620 --> 05:48:19,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Dahil nga, hindi sa lahat ng pagkakataon, ay readily nandyan bilang support system ang direct family.

6609
05:48:19,740 --> 05:48:25,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Gusto ko lang po natin marinig, bakit may ganitong partikular na sa BJMP lang?

6610
05:48:25,620 --> 05:48:35,120
BJMP Chief Jail Director Efren A. Nemeño: Mr. Chairman, Your Honor, hindi naman po namin pinagbabawal yung hindi direct family na bumisita sa jail facility natin.

6611
05:48:35,720 --> 05:48:46,880
BJMP Chief Jail Director Efren A. Nemeño: Ang pinahintulutan po natin yan, pag yung PDL po natin mismo, ay mag-allow sa person na yun na bibisita sa kanya.

6612
05:48:47,570 --> 05:48:56,660
BJMP Chief Jail Director Efren A. Nemeño: Hindi lang po natin ina-allow na automatic na pagdating doon, wala siyang, hindi naman in-allow ng PDL yun na bibisita ka sa kanya.

6613
05:48:57,210 --> 05:49:02,720
BJMP Chief Jail Director Efren A. Nemeño: Baka kasi, hindi naman gusto ng PDL yung tao na yun na bibisita sa kanya.

6614
05:49:02,820 --> 05:49:05,040
BJMP Chief Jail Director Efren A. Nemeño: Kaya, we need the clearance first.

6615
05:49:05,041 --> 05:49:11,200
BJMP Chief Jail Director Efren A. Nemeño: From the PDL na pwedeng bumisita sa kanya yung taong yun.

6616
05:49:11,201 --> 05:49:17,260
BJMP Chief Jail Director Efren A. Nemeño: Kaya kailangan, ilista niya yung name na yun, isubmit niya sa warden natin para makabisita sa kanya.

6617
05:49:18,620 --> 05:49:23,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ibig sabihin, kailangan, bago dumating kailangan, mayroon authorization muna sa bisita?

6618
05:49:23,840 --> 05:49:28,520
BJMP Chief Jail Director Efren A. Nemeño: Sabihin muna ng PDL po na ito, ina-allow kong magbibisita sa...

6619
05:49:28,520 --> 05:49:36,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Mr. Chair, hindi ba puwede na halimbawa, dumating doon, gustong makita yung PDL,

6620
05:49:37,300 --> 05:49:45,700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Edi simple lang naman yan eh, itatanong lang naman sa kanya kung okay ba sa iyo na may bumisita sa iyo?

6621
05:49:47,620 --> 05:49:50,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tama kayo, importante yung consent ng PDL.

6622
05:49:51,460 --> 05:49:55,980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero then and there, pwede naman tanungin siya, o gusto mo bang makita to?

6623
05:49:55,980 --> 05:50:03,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ito, pag sinabi niyang yes, hindi ba satisfied na?

6624
05:50:03,920 --> 05:50:05,800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Rather than, kailangan muna...

6625
05:50:06,780 --> 05:50:16,100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ilista niya. E paano niya malalaman? Halimbawa, may gustong, may grupo na gustong tumulong sa particular na individual na ito.

6626
05:50:16,560 --> 05:50:20,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: E hindi niya alam. Ito, paano niya marirequest yun?

6627
05:50:20,060 --> 05:50:22,280
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Can I interject with your indulgence?

6628
05:50:23,940 --> 05:50:29,840
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ang tinatanong siguro, ano ba yung guidelines niyo po? May written guidelines po ba kayo?

6629
05:50:30,240 --> 05:50:34,820
BJMP Chief Jail Director Efren A. Nemeño: May standard operating procedure, Mr. Chair, your honors, regarding that matter.

6630
05:50:34,820 --> 05:50:35,220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Okay.

6631
05:50:35,160 --> 05:50:36,880
BJMP Chief Jail Director Efren A. Nemeño: Direct family doctors.

6632
05:50:38,440 --> 05:50:42,580
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Can you submit your standard operating procedure to this committee?

6633
05:50:42,880 --> 05:50:43,940
BJMP Chief Jail Director Efren A. Nemeño: Yes, Mr. Chairman.

6634
05:50:44,080 --> 05:50:45,340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So that I can furnish also?

6635
05:50:46,240 --> 05:50:47,270
BJMP Chief Jail Director Efren A. Nemeño: Yes, Congressman.

6636
05:50:47,280 --> 05:51:02,700
BJMP Chief Jail Director Efren A. Nemeño: But we are very willing to listen to those concerns, Mr. Chairman, Your Honor, and willing to sit down and study if we can make changes in our path.

6637
05:51:03,360 --> 05:51:06,820
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yeah, yung sinasabi ni Kong Tinio, part ba yun ng guidelines,

6638
05:51:06,980 --> 05:51:07,800
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: yung mga biglaan?

6639
05:51:08,880 --> 05:51:12,140
BJMP Chief Jail Director Efren A. Nemeño: Hindi po pwede yung biglaan, your honor, because...

6640
05:51:12,780 --> 05:51:13,500
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: What's the reason?

6641
05:51:13,880 --> 05:51:22,260
BJMP Chief Jail Director Efren A. Nemeño: Majority of our jail facilities are locked spaces for visitation, your honor.

6642
05:51:22,340 --> 05:51:25,520
BJMP Chief Jail Director Efren A. Nemeño: That’s why ang inaalaw lang talaga natin muna.

6643
05:51:27,620 --> 05:51:28,440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Siniset niyo yung...

6644
05:51:28,441 --> 05:51:32,960
BJMP Chief Jail Director Efren A. Nemeño: Yes, yung direct family at saka yung doctor at saka yung lawyers niya, Mr. Chairman, your honor.

6645
05:51:33,040 --> 05:51:36,240
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yeah, but submit yung standard operating procedure, please.

6646
05:51:36,280 --> 05:51:38,580
BJMP Chief Jail Director Efren A. Nemeño: Yes, we will submit, Mr. Chairman.

6647
05:51:38,820 --> 05:51:40,420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Thank you for that, Chair.

6648
05:51:40,900 --> 05:51:46,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Maraming salamat po for requesting the written guidelines or standard operating procedures.

6649
05:51:46,820 --> 05:51:55,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Thank you rin kay director for openness to reviewing such guidelines.

6650
05:51:55,660 --> 05:52:05,900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang gusto lang po natin ibalance, of course, sabi niyo may mga considerations kayo, pero kailangan din yung kilalanin na may mga karapatan ng mga PDL.

6651
05:52:05,940 --> 05:52:06,980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So malinaw po ngayon.

6652
05:52:06,981 --> 05:52:11,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi ina-allow na biglaan may bumisita, talagang i-deny.

6653
05:52:12,880 --> 05:52:16,840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So kailangan talaga nakalista ng PDL.

6654
05:52:17,400 --> 05:52:22,720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero para sa amin, deprivation of rights yun.

6655
05:52:23,500 --> 05:52:32,080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Lalo pa, itong mga individual nga na to, ano pa naman eh, innocent, kahit nga yung mga convicted, may karapatan eh.

6656
05:52:32,160 --> 05:52:35,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, another topic.

6657
05:52:35,660 --> 05:52:36,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kanina po...

6658
05:52:36,560 --> 05:52:51,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Wala na po si Secretary Remulla, pero he spoke about procurement of fire trucks, 1,500 fire trucks, G2G with Korea.

6659
05:52:51,600 --> 05:52:52,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nabanggit niya yun.

6660
05:52:52,881 --> 05:53:02,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At nabanggit din niya yung context na talagang matagal nang controversial ang issue ng fire truck procurement sa BFP.

6661
05:53:03,420 --> 05:53:06,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: In the previous Congress, alam ko...

6662
05:53:07,000 --> 05:53:12,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ito na may ongoing investigation, may committee investigation dyan.

6663
05:53:12,520 --> 05:53:20,360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Because nga controversial yung on the part of BFP pati yung mga contractors involved.

6664
05:53:21,220 --> 05:53:21,460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, so...

6665
05:53:21,460 --> 05:53:33,100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang request na lang po natin ay, ano po ba ang status nung binanggit ni Secretary Remulia?

6666
05:53:33,840 --> 05:53:36,720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pinal na ba ito? May napirmahan na? May kontrata na?

6667
05:53:38,160 --> 05:53:40,080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Awarded na ba? Meron na bang mga...

6668
05:53:40,081 --> 05:53:50,680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sino yung mga contractors? Sino yung mga providers? Both on the part of Korea and the Philippines?

6669
05:53:54,000 --> 05:53:57,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sino po ang pwedeng magbigay ng update and information?

6670
05:53:57,860 --> 05:53:58,700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Just a sec, Paolo.

6671
05:53:58,701 --> 05:54:01,200
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: Thank you, Mr. Chair, Your Honor.

6672
05:54:01,200 --> 05:54:01,700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Kindly.

6673
05:54:01,200 --> 05:54:04,000
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: Thank you, Mr. Chair, Your Honor.

6674
05:54:04,000 --> 05:54:08,200
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: Insofar as the proposed government-to-government procurement,

6675
05:54:08,520 --> 05:54:10,540
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: fire trucks with the Republic of Korea,

6676
05:54:10,541 --> 05:54:13,360
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: the department is having advanced discussions with the relevant agencies

6677
05:54:13,361 --> 05:54:17,240
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: with the relevant agencies like the National Fire Agency of Korea,

6678
05:54:17,500 --> 05:54:20,100
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: the Korea Fire Institute, and most especially po,

6679
05:54:20,180 --> 05:54:24,820
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: the Korea Trade and Investment Promotion Agency or the KOTRA.

6680
05:54:25,540 --> 05:54:29,880
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: Sila po kasi talaga yung mag-open po ng bid po niyan.

6681
05:54:30,280 --> 05:54:31,860
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: They will conduct evaluation.

6682
05:54:32,340 --> 05:54:37,420
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: They will constitute two committees to screen the proposed suppliers.

6683
05:54:37,421 --> 05:54:43,980
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: Based on the technical specifications that will be provided po by the Philippines to them.

6684
05:54:43,980 --> 05:54:48,120
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: And then once, ano po yan, na-vet pa po nila yan,

6685
05:54:48,260 --> 05:54:50,440
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: they will send the recommendation of the suppliers.

6686
05:54:50,700 --> 05:54:53,420
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: Wala pa pong suppliers na ina-identify ang Philippines

6687
05:54:53,421 --> 05:54:57,600
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: because it will be the Korean government which will screen po itong mga suppliers.

6688
05:54:58,780 --> 05:55:07,780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So just to be clear, the suppliers will be identified by the Korean side,

6689
05:55:07,880 --> 05:55:08,720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: the Korean government?

6690
05:55:09,000 --> 05:55:09,480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Paano ba yun?

6691
05:55:09,480 --> 05:55:12,500
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: Based on the specifications that we will submit po.

6692
05:55:09,480 --> 05:55:11,240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Specifications to be provided by the Philippine government.

6693
05:55:14,720 --> 05:55:17,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So ang suppliers will be Korean suppliers?

6694
05:55:17,920 --> 05:55:19,460
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: Tama po, Mr. Chair.

6695
05:55:19,540 --> 05:55:24,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Meron bang role dito yung mga Philippine contractors?

6696
05:55:25,160 --> 05:55:26,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yun yung isang concern natin eh.

6697
05:55:26,780 --> 05:55:27,080
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: Wala po.

6698
05:55:27,081 --> 05:55:31,620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung mga contractors na involved na in many controversial issues.

6699
05:55:32,080 --> 05:55:32,600
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: Wala po.

6700
05:55:32,720 --> 05:55:35,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So Korean ang supplier, ganun po ba?

6701
05:55:35,360 --> 05:55:36,340
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: Tama po, Mr. Chair.

6702
05:55:36,340 --> 05:55:38,560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: However, the status is, it is still

6703
05:55:38,560 --> 05:55:40,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: under negotiation, ganun po ba?

6704
05:55:40,520 --> 05:55:43,420
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: Right now po, we are refining the technical specifications

6705
05:55:43,421 --> 05:55:49,760
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: after po nung makita po namin yung mga available specs ng fire trucks in Korea.

6706
05:55:50,940 --> 05:55:53,880
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: Ina-adapt po based din sa need ng BFP,

6707
05:55:53,980 --> 05:55:58,040
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: like lalagyan din po ng mga rescue equipment po yung fire trucks natin.

6708
05:55:58,740 --> 05:55:59,380
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: Yun po.

6709
05:55:59,480 --> 05:56:02,260
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: And then after po ma-finalize po yung technical specifications,

6710
05:56:02,540 --> 05:56:06,000
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: and as I understand po, it will be submitted by the BFP by tomorrow,

6711
05:56:06,340 --> 05:56:07,200
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: So, yun ho, we will continue coordinating.

6712
05:56:07,340 --> 05:56:11,760
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: We will continue coordinating with the Republic of Korea on this one.

6713
05:56:11,760 --> 05:56:12,160
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: With KOTRA.

6714
05:56:11,900 --> 05:56:23,780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Chair, pwede pong makahingi na lang ng written update on the status of this possible procurement.

6715
05:56:24,020 --> 05:56:25,600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, can be submitted to this committee.

6716
05:56:26,040 --> 05:56:28,620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ASAP po sana bago tayo mag-plenaryo.

6717
05:56:28,620 --> 05:56:31,500
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Actually, just to explain further,

6718
05:56:32,200 --> 05:56:35,780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: kakapunta lang po nila ng Korea, I think, two weeks ago.

6719
05:56:36,340 --> 05:56:38,760
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, talking points pa lang.

6720
05:56:38,980 --> 05:56:40,240
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: How to process it, no?

6721
05:56:40,440 --> 05:56:43,040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And I asked also Secretary Jonvic,

6722
05:56:43,120 --> 05:56:44,760
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: why Korea, not Japan?

6723
05:56:45,100 --> 05:56:47,920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Mas mura yung Korea by 30%.

6724
05:56:47,921 --> 05:56:50,120
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, mas makakatipid pa tayo.

6725
05:56:50,140 --> 05:56:54,300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Plus, yung may supply rin yung Korea,

6726
05:56:54,560 --> 05:56:58,460
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: pag nasira, maintenance, sila rin.

6727
05:56:58,461 --> 05:56:59,400
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, kasama rin yun.

6728
05:56:59,640 --> 05:57:01,600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ang maganda lang is government to government,

6729
05:57:01,880 --> 05:57:05,140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: makawala na po yung mga sinasabi natin, mga SOP, etc.

6730
05:57:05,141 --> 05:57:08,260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But ang pinaka-importante is DBM,

6731
05:57:08,700 --> 05:57:12,440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: i-push natin, i-release yung pondo para sa Bureau of Fire

6732
05:57:12,441 --> 05:57:15,300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: para matapos itong problema sa ambulansya,

6733
05:57:15,400 --> 05:57:18,440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: pati po sa ating problema sa ating fire station,

6734
05:57:18,740 --> 05:57:24,280
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: problema rin po na 40,000 na mga personnel na kulang sila.

6735
05:57:24,360 --> 05:57:26,760
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, yun po talaga ang solusyon.

6736
05:57:26,761 --> 05:57:28,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Thank you, Sec.

6737
05:57:28,700 --> 05:57:29,800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: I mean, Kong.

6738
05:57:32,740 --> 05:57:33,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Wiro lang po.

6739
05:57:33,560 --> 05:57:34,590
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Thank you, Chair.

6740
05:57:35,792 --> 05:57:37,060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, we hope ma-submit po,

6741
05:57:37,061 --> 05:57:40,180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: bago mag-plenaryo, ang kanilang update.

6742
05:57:40,420 --> 05:57:41,800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Detailed update.

6743
05:57:42,020 --> 05:57:42,580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Thank you po.

6744
05:57:42,720 --> 05:57:43,420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you.

6745
05:57:44,420 --> 05:57:47,900
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Next, last to interpellate from the minority,

6746
05:57:48,200 --> 05:57:50,420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: ang aking anak din.

6747
05:57:52,420 --> 05:57:53,960
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Hinahanapan ko pong asawa 'to.

6748
05:57:54,860 --> 05:57:56,140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Attorney Renee Co.

6749
05:57:56,141 --> 05:57:57,720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Congresswoman Renee Co, please.

6750
05:57:57,721 --> 05:58:01,380
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Grabe na yung pagre-reto sa national stage.

6751
05:58:01,381 --> 05:58:02,260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Sige po.

6752
05:58:02,261 --> 05:58:04,500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you very much, Mr. Chair.

6753
05:58:04,501 --> 05:58:06,920
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Gusto ko lang pong mag-take off sa ilan.

6754
05:58:07,260 --> 05:58:09,820
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ang mga questions na natanong ko kanina

6755
05:58:09,821 --> 05:58:11,620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and then ng tanong ng ibang representatives.

6756
05:58:11,621 --> 05:58:16,380
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, meron pong na-mention si Secretary kanina,

6757
05:58:16,381 --> 05:58:20,020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: yung drug war, hindi na nga po policy yan,

6758
05:58:20,021 --> 05:58:22,620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: or yung Oplan Tokhang for the past four years.

6759
05:58:22,840 --> 05:58:26,880
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Pero, unfortunately, ay nagpapatuloy pa rin yung arbitrary listing.

6760
05:58:27,180 --> 05:58:29,740
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ito po yung reports na nakukuha natin on the ground.

6761
05:58:30,020 --> 05:58:32,540
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Meron pong mga nasa listahan pa rin,

6762
05:58:32,541 --> 05:58:35,240
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: at the barangay level.

6763
05:58:35,500 --> 05:58:36,560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: For example,

6764
05:58:36,600 --> 05:58:37,680
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: si Jemboy Baltazar,

6765
05:58:37,681 --> 05:58:39,800
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: or in 2021, Caraga 2.

6766
05:58:40,020 --> 05:58:43,380
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: May mga journalists pong nahahalo pa rin sa listahan.

6767
05:58:43,660 --> 05:58:44,660
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mexico 4.

6768
05:58:44,880 --> 05:58:47,520
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And meron pa rin pong reports of reenacted arrests.

6769
05:58:47,521 --> 05:58:49,620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, ang tanong ko po,

6770
05:58:49,760 --> 05:58:53,040
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: kung natigil na nga po ang oplantokhang,

6771
05:58:53,041 --> 05:58:54,780
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: at sabi nga po,

6772
05:58:54,781 --> 05:58:58,040
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: community-based, health-centered approach na under VIDA,

6773
05:58:58,041 --> 05:59:00,740
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ang pag-address ng issue ng droga,

6774
05:59:00,820 --> 05:59:04,260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: bakit po tuloy-tuloy pa rin yung drug watch list system

6775
05:59:04,261 --> 05:59:05,400
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: at the barangay level?

6776
05:59:09,280 --> 05:59:10,840
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: Your Honor, Mr. Chair,

6777
05:59:11,000 --> 05:59:11,680
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: totoo po yan.

6778
05:59:12,980 --> 05:59:14,500
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: Katulad ng sinabi ko kanina,

6779
05:59:14,640 --> 05:59:18,040
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: as deputized agents of the

6780
05:59:18,041 --> 05:59:22,060
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: Philippine Drug Enforcement Agency,

6781
05:59:22,520 --> 05:59:24,260
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: ay meron po tayong programa.

6782
05:59:24,460 --> 05:59:27,240
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: And the program in our campaign against illegal drugs

6783
05:59:27,241 --> 05:59:30,740
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: is no less than the supply and demand reduction.

6784
05:59:30,741 --> 05:59:32,340
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: On the part of

6785
05:59:32,341 --> 05:59:34,740
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: sa demand reduction,

6786
05:59:35,040 --> 05:59:36,460
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: marami po tayong mga programa.

6787
05:59:36,461 --> 05:59:37,600
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: Like, for example,

6788
05:59:37,620 --> 05:59:39,620
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: we go with,

6789
05:59:39,630 --> 05:59:40,450
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: with the community.

6790
05:59:40,451 --> 05:59:47,480
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: The community in various campaign para maiwasan ang pagtangkil sa droga and the like.

6791
05:59:48,110 --> 05:59:59,840
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: And we are also on the front line with regards to the supply reduction, especially in the conduct of police operations.

6792
06:00:00,200 --> 06:00:19,120
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: The conduct of police operations, nagsisimula po yan one by one painstakingly sa the conduct of information and intelligence gathering such that meron po tayong probable person of interest or target.

6793
06:00:19,300 --> 06:00:29,460
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: At yan po ang pinupuso natin. And that is why meron po tayong minimaintain na persons of interest or target person.

6794
06:00:29,940 --> 06:00:49,760
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: These target personalities came from doon sa mga nahuhuli na mismo natin, those who have been arrested based on interview and based on the arrests that were made in the last several years.

6795
06:00:49,761 --> 06:00:56,880
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: At tuloy-tuloy po yun. And so that's how we maintain our list. That's why we have our list.

6796
06:00:57,300 --> 06:00:59,320
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, Mr. Chair, confirmation na may nagtutuloy at nagkocontinue na drug watch list system at barangay level.

6797
06:01:00,060 --> 06:01:06,080
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: May nagtutuloy at nagkocontinue na parang drug watch list system at labarangay level.

6798
06:01:06,380 --> 06:01:12,840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So siguro talawang tanong na lang po, paano po na-verify yung mga individuals na to?

6799
06:01:13,020 --> 06:01:17,940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: You mentioned a process, pero ano po siguro yung pagdetalye? Paano nagagawa yun?

6800
06:01:17,941 --> 06:01:24,920
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And number two, kunwari rehabilitated na ano yung recourse nila para matanggal?

6801
06:01:25,120 --> 06:01:29,540
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Dahil ang dulo naman po nito, wini-welcome natin yung health center.

6802
06:01:29,980 --> 06:01:38,880
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Approach, rehabilitation, yan yan. Ay gusto natin we target the supply and hindi yung down to yung parang low level demand, diba?

6803
06:01:39,860 --> 06:01:42,720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ano po yung siguro-sagot doon, Mr. Chair?

6804
06:01:42,721 --> 06:01:49,220
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: Your Honor, Mr. Chair, we follow certain procedures especially in the adjudication.

6805
06:01:49,221 --> 06:01:58,540
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: And sinusunod po natin, especially in the conduct of police operations, marami na pong ibinigay, lalo ng Court Suprema,

6806
06:01:58,541 --> 06:01:59,380
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: to ensure.

6807
06:01:59,381 --> 06:02:11,860
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: Na wala pong EGK or wala po tayong sinasabing SBI system or whatsoever.

6808
06:02:12,720 --> 06:02:16,180
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: Ang ginagawa mo natin ay an intelligence-driven police operation.

6809
06:02:16,620 --> 06:02:19,000
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: Nandyan po ang ating body-worn camera.

6810
06:02:19,920 --> 06:02:27,980
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: Nandyan po ang ating masticating or ating mga witnesses in the conduct of a police operation.

6811
06:02:28,360 --> 06:02:29,560
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: This is being...

6812
06:02:29,561 --> 06:02:33,680
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: adhered to by our police officers, especially the PNP.

6813
06:02:33,860 --> 06:02:35,260
PNP Chief Police General Jose Melencio C. Nartatez Jr.: Your Honor, Mr. Chair.

6814
06:02:35,261 --> 06:02:41,940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Chair, ano po bang systemic administrative sanctions ang na-impose na ng DILG-NAPOLCOM

6815
06:02:41,941 --> 06:02:47,820
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: against police personnel that were involved in botched operations, reenacted arrests, and even sa EGK?

6816
06:02:48,580 --> 06:02:50,440
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ano pong update dito, Mr. Chair?

6817
06:02:50,640 --> 06:02:51,180
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: NAPOLCOM?

6818
06:02:51,980 --> 06:02:52,580
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: NAPOLCOM?

6819
06:02:55,540 --> 06:02:58,780
NAPOLCOM Vice Chairperson and Executive Officer Atty. Rafael Vicente R. Calinisan: Tuloy-tuloy po ang ating investigations, ma'am.

6820
06:02:58,840 --> 06:03:01,640
NAPOLCOM Vice Chairperson and Executive Officer Atty. Rafael Vicente R. Calinisan: As we have discussed before and narinig ninyo naman po.

6821
06:03:03,840 --> 06:03:06,020
NAPOLCOM Vice Chairperson and Executive Officer Atty. Rafael Vicente R. Calinisan: We have zero backlog for cases.

6822
06:03:06,480 --> 06:03:11,240
NAPOLCOM Vice Chairperson and Executive Officer Atty. Rafael Vicente R. Calinisan: Lahat naman po nang nakita natin na kailangan imbestigahan, ay ginagawa naman po natin.

6823
06:03:11,300 --> 06:03:13,340
NAPOLCOM Vice Chairperson and Executive Officer Atty. Rafael Vicente R. Calinisan: We are mindful of certain things.

6824
06:03:13,341 --> 06:03:24,940
NAPOLCOM Vice Chairperson and Executive Officer Atty. Rafael Vicente R. Calinisan: But, as assured, Mr. Chair, that the National Police Commission is very much active and willing to take on any challenge pag may ganyan pong concern.

6825
06:03:25,120 --> 06:03:25,840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Chair?

6826
06:03:25,940 --> 06:03:31,780
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Chair, puwede po bang makapagsubmit ang NAPOLCOM ng Disciplinary Action Status Report for 2025?

6827
06:03:31,781 --> 06:03:33,420
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: 2026, detailing yung mga administrative charges, summary dismissals, conviction records, etc.

6828
06:03:33,690 --> 06:03:35,870
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, you're hereby directed to submit.

6829
06:03:35,880 --> 06:03:39,700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Summary dismissals, conviction records, etc.

6830
06:03:40,020 --> 06:03:42,520
NAPOLCOM Vice Chairperson and Executive Officer Atty. Rafael Vicente R. Calinisan: No problem po, Mr. Chair.

6831
06:03:42,700 --> 06:03:52,920
NAPOLCOM Vice Chairperson and Executive Officer Atty. Rafael Vicente R. Calinisan: But siguro po, to inform you po, we have zero case backlog for the past 25 years.

6832
06:03:54,200 --> 06:03:57,940
NAPOLCOM Vice Chairperson and Executive Officer Atty. Rafael Vicente R. Calinisan: Inubos na po natin yan. And all the cases being heard by the NAPOLCOM right now are current cases.

6833
06:03:58,400 --> 06:04:00,320
NAPOLCOM Vice Chairperson and Executive Officer Atty. Rafael Vicente R. Calinisan: Wala na po tayong pending, Mr. Chair.

6834
06:04:00,440 --> 06:04:01,840
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Okay, but kindly submit.

6835
06:04:02,380 --> 06:04:04,000
NAPOLCOM Vice Chairperson and Executive Officer Atty. Rafael Vicente R. Calinisan: We will submit po, Mr. Chair.

6836
06:04:04,080 --> 06:04:04,440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you.

6837
06:04:04,660 --> 06:04:05,380
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: By when?

6838
06:04:05,720 --> 06:04:06,740
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

6839
06:04:06,940 --> 06:04:07,620
NAPOLCOM Vice Chairperson and Executive Officer Atty. Rafael Vicente R. Calinisan: As soon as possible.

6840
06:04:08,180 --> 06:04:09,740
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: What is as soon as possible?

6841
06:04:10,260 --> 06:04:11,920
NAPOLCOM Vice Chairperson and Executive Officer Atty. Rafael Vicente R. Calinisan: Kahit po, Monday.

6842
06:04:12,380 --> 06:04:13,880
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Wow, that's fast. Holiday.

6843
06:04:14,420 --> 06:04:15,660
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Make it Tuesday, sir.

6844
06:04:16,160 --> 06:04:16,860
NAPOLCOM Vice Chairperson and Executive Officer Atty. Rafael Vicente R. Calinisan: Tuesday po.

6845
06:04:17,480 --> 06:04:18,040
NAPOLCOM Vice Chairperson and Executive Officer Atty. Rafael Vicente R. Calinisan: Thank you.

6846
06:04:18,041 --> 06:04:19,920
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Happy National Heroes Day sa atin.

6847
06:04:20,160 --> 06:04:21,740
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, thank you, Mr. Chair.

6848
06:04:21,940 --> 06:04:25,940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: My next question is in relation po to the Barangay Development Program.

6849
06:04:27,640 --> 06:04:30,540
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Dahil from last year,

6850
06:04:30,620 --> 06:04:35,260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: naging parang 10 million per barangay, naging 5 million na lang per barangay.

6851
06:04:35,261 --> 06:04:38,560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And dumami po yung mga barangay na beneficiaries neto.

6852
06:04:38,980 --> 06:04:44,220
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: May tanong ko, ano po bang actual physical and financial accomplishment rate

6853
06:04:44,221 --> 06:04:49,080
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ng Barangay Development Program na bilyong piso po talaga yung nailalaan dito?

6854
06:04:49,820 --> 06:04:52,980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And paano po na-audit ng DILG?

6855
06:04:52,981 --> 06:04:57,860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At nabiverify yung authenticity ng ECLIP beneficiaries?

6856
06:04:58,010 --> 06:04:58,520
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Yes.

6857
06:04:59,860 --> 06:05:02,380
DILG Undersecretary for Local Government Marlo L. Iringan: Thank you, Mr. Chair. I will reply to that. The DILG is only one of the many agencies under the Ending Local Communist Armed Conflict Task Force, and the responsibility of the DILG is to facilitate the consultation at the barangay level between and among the people and barangay officials so that they can identify priority programs funded by the Barangay Development Program.

6858
06:05:28,680 --> 06:05:55,560
DILG Undersecretary for Local Government Marlo L. Iringan: For 2021, the delivery rate is 99.86%. For 2022, it's 100%. For 2023, it's 98.48%. For 2024, dun sa original na allocation, 2.5 million, it's 90%. And then there's an additional 5 million which was given towards the third quarter or last quarter of the year. The delivery rate is 71%.

6859
06:05:55,561 --> 06:06:14,900
DILG Undersecretary for Local Government Marlo L. Iringan: For 2025, our performance is at the level of 29%. For 2026, wala pong completed na project. As much as the fund was released only the second quarter and the third quarter of this year, Mr. Chair.

6860
06:06:15,520 --> 06:06:19,900
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Can these documents be submitted to the representation, Mr. Chair?

6861
06:06:20,320 --> 06:06:23,560
DILG Undersecretary for Local Government Marlo L. Iringan: Gladly, Mr. Chair. We will provide a copy to the committee.

6862
06:06:23,960 --> 06:06:25,300
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So yung tanong ko rin po sa...

6863
06:06:25,301 --> 06:06:42,560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ...na isang bahagi. Paano po nagiging bahagi yung DILG? Ano pong ginagawa ng DILG to audit and verify yung authenticity? So isang bahagi yung distribution, di ba po? Pero pagkatapos na na-distribute, paano po na-insure na nagigamit po yun sa purposes stated?

6864
06:06:44,520 --> 06:06:55,100
DILG Undersecretary for Local Government Marlo L. Iringan: Yung support to Barangay Development Program is lumped under the Local Government Support Fund. And for this purpose, the DILG was given the responsibility to do the monitoring and evaluation.

6865
06:06:55,580 --> 06:07:15,600
DILG Undersecretary for Local Government Marlo L. Iringan: And as mentioned by the Secretary a while ago, we hired, at this time, 700 engineers and program evaluation officers to monitor not only the SBDP, this fund, but also the other financial assistance to local government units, the growth equity fund, which are under the LGSF, Mr. Chair.

6866
06:07:15,700 --> 06:07:25,740
DILG Undersecretary for Local Government Marlo L. Iringan: So we have people on the ground to make sure that these projects are implemented accordingly, and we require our local government units to upload...

6867
06:07:25,741 --> 06:07:33,860
DILG Undersecretary for Local Government Marlo L. Iringan: ...the progress status of the projects in the Subay Bayan portal regularly, Mr. Chair.

6868
06:07:33,861 --> 06:07:51,160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ang re-report po natin, Mr. Chair, ay meron po tayong advocates that wish to access yung mga relevant documents nga po. Yan, for example, ASARO on the website. Pero unfortunately, ay hindi po siya available. Parang last year, kayang ma-access yung ilang documents, pero this year ay hindi na po.

6869
06:07:51,320 --> 06:07:55,860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So ayaw natin magkaroon ng sitwasyon.

6870
06:07:55,861 --> 06:08:10,660
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Kung saan hindi po kaya ma-scrutinize ng mamamayan, maging bahagi ng paano ba na-ensure na yung pondo ng gobyerno galing sa pera ng mamamayan ay hindi po na-account kung saan na pupunta.

6871
06:08:10,860 --> 06:08:25,640
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But you mentioned po, may engineers, etc. So may audit processes po ang DILG dito. So maaari po bang makapagsubmit ang DILG ng full financial and physical performance audit ng funds under BDP?

6872
06:08:25,641 --> 06:08:29,580
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And yung disbursement breakdown ng ECLIP for the last year, Mr. Chair?

6873
06:08:29,581 --> 06:08:44,720
DILG Undersecretary for Local Government Marlo L. Iringan: Yes, Mr. Chair. What we can provide is the status of the physical project completion and the fund releases. As to the scrutiny of how the funds are used, we leave it to the Commission on Audit.

6874
06:08:44,721 --> 06:08:52,620
DILG Undersecretary for Local Government Marlo L. Iringan: I also would like to add, Mr. Chair, that the SBDP projects are subject to third-party monitoring.

6875
06:08:53,660 --> 06:08:54,820
DILG Undersecretary for Local Government Marlo L. Iringan: We have...

6876
06:08:54,821 --> 06:09:01,160
DILG Undersecretary for Local Government Marlo L. Iringan: ...coordinated with the CSOs and NGOs to help us monitor the implementation of the SBDP projects.

6877
06:09:01,640 --> 06:09:07,140
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And to clarify, yung third-party na in-engage to monitor, ang DILG po ang nag-engage sa kanya?

6878
06:09:08,120 --> 06:09:16,700
DILG Undersecretary for Local Government Marlo L. Iringan: Yes, Mr. Chair, but there's a sort of criteria in determining the third-party monitor.

6879
06:09:17,560 --> 06:09:25,420
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So is the DILG also a recipient of the reports of this third-party in its monitoring? Baka po pwedeng masubmit din po iyon sa committee?

6880
06:09:25,800 --> 06:09:35,060
DILG Undersecretary for Local Government Marlo L. Iringan: Yes, Mr. Chair. We, naturally, we are the first group which benefit from the report of the third-party monitors.

6881
06:09:35,220 --> 06:09:38,080
DILG Undersecretary for Local Government Marlo L. Iringan: And we would gladly provide you a copy of the report.

6882
06:09:38,280 --> 06:09:39,200
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you. By when?

6883
06:09:39,560 --> 06:09:40,460
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

6884
06:09:40,600 --> 06:09:41,020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: By when?

6885
06:09:43,560 --> 06:09:44,000
DILG Undersecretary for Local Government Marlo L. Iringan: When?

6886
06:09:44,000 --> 06:09:44,440
DILG Undersecretary for Local Government Marlo L. Iringan: Tuesday?

6887
06:09:45,220 --> 06:09:46,540
DILG Undersecretary for Local Government Marlo L. Iringan: Next week, Mr. Chair. Tuesday.

6888
06:09:46,680 --> 06:09:47,300
DILG Undersecretary for Local Government Marlo L. Iringan: Thank you.

6889
06:09:47,900 --> 06:09:49,060
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

6890
06:09:49,420 --> 06:09:56,220
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: My next question is in relation naman po sa active shooting drills that na-announce po, supposedly this week mangyayari pero na-push back po to September.

6891
06:09:56,221 --> 06:09:57,320
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Supposedly, this week...

6892
06:10:00,700 --> 06:10:08,500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: May I ask kung meron na po bang comprehensive plan and timeline kung paano po ito isasagawa sa bansa?

6893
06:10:09,520 --> 06:10:11,920
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Bahagi po ba ang DILG sa pagplano po nito, Mr. Chair?

6894
06:10:13,820 --> 06:10:14,900
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: Mr. Chair, may I?

6895
06:10:15,620 --> 06:10:22,020
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: The DepEd po is spearheading this. It will be a school-led event and they have issued guidelines.

6896
06:10:22,021 --> 06:10:27,660
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: And they are coordinating with the PNP, the DILG, and the BFP so far as the drills are concerned.

6897
06:10:28,100 --> 06:10:31,940
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: Ang plan po dito is they will conduct simulation drills in schools.

6898
06:10:31,941 --> 06:10:38,920
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: And then there will be a group of experts like, for example, members from the PNP, DILG,

6899
06:10:38,921 --> 06:10:43,880
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: which will somehow comment on how the drills are being conducted.

6900
06:10:44,320 --> 06:10:50,460
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: Right now, the guidelines po are being refined by the DepEd in coordination with the DILG regional offices

6901
06:10:50,880 --> 06:10:54,460
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: and then mga PNP personnel po natin sa regions.

6902
06:10:54,820 --> 06:10:57,320
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: And then as soon as the guidelines are finished,

6903
06:10:57,640 --> 06:11:03,340
DILG Undersecretary for Plans and Programs Jon Paulo V. Salvahan: we will resume with the, we will schedule the drills.

